_default — fallback handler for unknown $ externals

SUMMARY
  Used when $name is not registered in externals/__init__.py _KNOWN set.
  Does not implement real logic; appends a placeholder texts[] entry so
  pipelines can be written before a dedicated handler exists.

SYNTAX
  $any_unknown_name
  $any_unknown_name(arg='value')

INPUT
  Full bundle copied through.

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one new link: "[emulated $name]"

BEHAVIOR
  Dispatched automatically by externals.run_external via
  externals._default.run. To add a real external, create externals/<name>/run.py
  and register <name> in _KNOWN.

EXAMPLE
  @bad_image_quality: $image_filter
  (until externals/image_filter/ is implemented)

NOTE
  This folder is not a user-facing $ call; it is the runtime fallback only.
